Introduction 
         Front-end development is the process of designing the visual and interactive components of web applications and websites—the components consumers see and interact with straight away in their web browsers. Beginners who wish to learn how to create modern, responsive websites using fundamental web technology will find this course suitable. 
  
  The course front-end development covers three basic languages: 
  
  HTML (HyperText Markup Language) is used for content structuring. 
  
  Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) provide layout and design options. 
  
  JavaScript for dynamic content and interactivity. 
  
  Students will also investigate tools and frameworks that facilitate quicker and simpler development, including as code editors, version control (Git), and well-known libraries like React and Bootstrap. 
  
  Learners will be able by course's end to create and publish a simple but functional website, know web page structure, use design, and add interactivity to improve user experience.

What is front end development course?
A front-end development course teaches individuals the skills and knowledge necessary to create the user-facing part of websites and web applications. This includes learning to build interfaces, design layouts, and add interactive elements using languages like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Courses often cover responsive design, UI/UX principles, and frameworks like React or Angular. 
